description.narrative:
Reform area: Reform Area 2: Quality of Public Expenditure and Cash Management Improved 

Outcome: e. Fiscal deficit-to-GDP ratio narrowed to 4.0% to gradually bring it in line with the legislative threshold of 3.5% for promoting fiscal sustainability set out in the FRDLA, 2005 (FY2021 Baseline: 7.1% of GDP).
Source: Ministry of Finance (MOF). 

Description: 2.5	To improve efficiency of public expenditure management and conclude the operationalization of the PFM Act 2019 (amended 2020):
(i)	Federal cabinet has approved and FD has notified compiled General Finance Rules, including updates to system of financial management, revenue receipt mechanism, budgeting, inventory management, and government accounting to ensure the operationalization of the PFM Act 2019 (amended 2020);
(ii)	Federal cabinet has approved and FD has notified rules for management and control of Special Purpose Funds to ensure efficient management of public moneys appropriated to such funds established under any law or with the approval of the Federal Government;
(iii)	Federal cabinet has approved and FD has notified Federal Treasury (Receipt and Payment) Rules;
(iv)	Federal cabinet has approved and FD has notified Grant-in-Aid Rules to provide a formal framework for the management of moneys given by the Federal Government to public and private entities;
(v)	FD has established Cash Management and Forecasting Unit and assigned responsible for issuing regular and accurate monthly and quarterly cash forecasts to allow for more effective cash management; and
(vi)	FD has submitedsubmitted the annual budget statement for FY2025 to the National Assembly reflecting funds deposited in the Federal Consolidated Account by the relevant ministries, departments and agencies, and Public Entities disaggregated by the source to allow the National Assembly to assess the effectiveness of cash consolidation reforms.
Documentation required: (i) Cabinet approval and notified General Finance Rules, (ii) notified Special Purpose Funds Rules, (iii) notified Federal Treasury (Receipt and Payment) Rules, (iv) notified Grant-in-Aid Rules, (v) Finance Division&apos;s notification on establishment of CM&FU, and (vi) published Explanatory Memorandum on Federal Receipt on Finance Division&apos; website.
